From: mayi <3363523343@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:28:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] perf(wifi): quiet startup console and wake on validated handshake

[description ]:
- Route routine Linux RHEA SDIO startup messages to KERN_DEBUG and keep
  bound, accepted timing and real backend readiness as KERN_INFO records.
- Keep genuine error-level atbm_dbg calls on the error path.
- Replace the BF01 fixed startup sleep with a wait on the existing WSM
  queue, woken after successful parsing and validation of the indication.

[root   cause]:
- Routine initialization banners use KERN_ERR and remain synchronous
  console traffic with the board's loglevel=4 at 115200 baud.
- The startup waiter sleeps for 20 ms even when the real indication has
  already arrived; firmwareReady is published before final validation.
- The measured successful attempt waits only 50 ms, with much of the
  boot-to-live latency before driver initialization, not in retry waits.

[JIRA      ID]:N/A (BF01 integration)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- Applies after the latest 0042. Keeps bus recovery, function checks,
  IRQ polling, cancellation, shutdown and the 1000 ms timeout/retry policy.
- Normal INIT messages remain in dmesg, not the default serial console.
  Error-level atbm_dbg routing is shared; event waiting is BF01-only.
- No application, cloud parameter, AI, media, pinmux or power-policy change.
- No board deployment, forced unload or hot reload. Physical latency gain
  and live/AI/shutdown regression still require real board measurements.
[test]:
- Matching Linux 5.10 ARM module build; 183 isolated source-derived startup
  and indication cases with UBSan, plus BF01/other-platform log checks.
- Isolated controls use mock transport, not hardware/business acceptance.

---
diff --git a/extdrv/wireless/realtek/atbm6461/hal_apollo/debug.h b/extdrv/wireless/realtek/atbm6461/hal_apollo/debug.h
--- a/extdrv/wireless/realtek/atbm6461/hal_apollo/debug.h
+++ b/extdrv/wireless/realtek/atbm6461/hal_apollo/debug.h
@@ -33,9 +33,14 @@
 #define FUNC_EXIT() //printk("%s %d--\n",__func__,__LINE__)
 
 
-#define atbm_dbg(level, ...)				\
- if ((level) & ATBM_APOLLO_DBG_LEVEL)		\
-		atbm_printk_init(__VA_ARGS__);	\
+#define atbm_dbg(level, ...) do { \
+	if ((level) & ATBM_APOLLO_DBG_LEVEL) { \
+		if ((level) & ATBM_APOLLO_DBG_ERROR) \
+			atbm_printk_err(__VA_ARGS__); \
+		else \
+			atbm_printk_init(__VA_ARGS__); \
+	} \
+} while (0)
 
 extern u32 atbm_control_debug_mask;
 
@@ -76,6 +81,16 @@
 #define atbm_printk_err(...) 		atbm_printk(ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_ERR,__VA_ARGS__)
 #define atbm_printk_warn(...)		atbm_printk(ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_WARN,__VA_ARGS__)
 #define atbm_printk_init(...)		atbm_printk(ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_INIT,__VA_ARGS__)
+#if defined(LINUX_OS) && (PROJ_TYPE == RHEA) && defined(SDIO_BUS)
+#undef atbm_printk_init
+#define atbm_printk_init(fmt, arg...) do { \
+	if (atbm_printk_mask & ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_INIT) \
+		printk(KERN_DEBUG ATBM_TAG fmt, ##arg); \
+} while (0)
+#define atbm_printk_boot(...)		atbm_printk_init(__VA_ARGS__)
+#else
+#define atbm_printk_boot(...)		atbm_printk_always(__VA_ARGS__)
+#endif
 #define atbm_printk_exit(...)		atbm_printk(ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_EXIT,__VA_ARGS__)
 #define atbm_printk_bus(...)		atbm_printk(ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_BUS,__VA_ARGS__)
 #define atbm_printk_scan(...)		atbm_printk(ATBM_PRINTK_MASK_SCAN,__VA_ARGS__)
